  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This soundboard recording captures Mountain Goats performing fifteen songs at Will’s Pub in Orlando, Florida, on February 20, 2004 [1]. The setlist includes “Slow West Vultures,” “Southwood Plantation Road,” and “International Small Arms Traffic Blues” [1]. Later in the show, the band plays “Linda Blair Was Born Innocent,” “Jaipur,” and “The Young Thousands” [1]. The track “Cotton” is the earliest version of that song available in the archive [1]. The performance continues with “Jenny,” “Palmcorder Yajna,” and “Your Belgian Things” [1]. The final songs are “It Froze Me,” “Baboon,” “Quito,” “No Children,” and “The Mess Inside” [1]. The total runtime is approximately fifty-three minutes [1]. This is the only recording of this specific show in the archive [1]. It is the fifty-fourth show in the archive’s collection for the band [2]. The previous archived show was on February 18, 2004, at The EARL [2]. The audio was captured using a Sony MZ-R70 MiniDisc recorder [1]. Doors opened at 9:00 PM with an eight-dollar cover charge for those eighteen and older [1]. The file is part of a master dump of live music from Orlando between 2000 and 2005 [1].",
